Quick judgement on RAGE_QUIT_99 typing in ALL CAPS

My read: more likely an angry kid / human than a lazy bot — but bots can be scripted to shout. ALL CAPS alone doesn’t prove human; it’s a common stylistic flag used by both people and cheap bot scripts.

How to tell: a human will mix caps with grammatical fragments, emojis, context-specific anger (“wtf map RNG” / “that lag was trash”), and variable timing. A bot will likely post CAPS mechanically (same phrasing across matches), often immediately after an event.

If you want believable rage: use context-aware rants (mention weapon/map/time), add typos, and randomize timing (delay 1–6s, then partial messages like “fuck—” then full message).

Global problems that make the pool feel botty

Homogenous archetype density: too many “rager” variants with same bio tone. Real populations are noisy — not 25 clones of the same simmering rage.

Name patterns: Xx_ wrappers, numeric suffixes (99, 42) and ALL-CAPS names concentrated in one archetype.

Win rate / rank mismatch: several Bronzes with mid-high win rates and Golds with improbably consistent 70+ — looks tuned, not natural.

Avatar reuse and emoji overreliance: repeated emojis map too cleanly to archetype.

Bios feel templated: 90% are 2–3 word punchlines or meme phrases; real players vary length, style, grammar, punctuation, and topic.

Concrete fixes to make them believable (do these, not optional)

Diversify name formats — mix: firstname/lastname-style handles, regional names, short nicknames, casual phrases, and occasional leetspeak. Example set: TariqPlays, mari., roninLuke, Jas_94, mama’s_boy (yes, the last is human).

Vary bios length & tone — add: short personal lines, game-specific gripes, inside jokes, casual complaints, life noises. Examples:

“always sniping from the roof — pls nerf”

“mic broke, sry”

“studying for finals rn, playing on off-hours”

include typos and emojis sparingly.

Win rate vs rank realism — create distribution: Gold: 55–75, Silver: 45–65, Bronze: 25–50. Don’t pack Gold with 70–78 for everything. Add variance over time (simulate streaks).

Chat behavior templates — implement per-archetype message pools with variability & context-sensitivity. Example rager lines (vary casing, punctuation, typos):

“wtf that was a hitbox”

“bro LAG”

“i’m done. gg”

“NO WAY i got sniped from behind???”
Also: add pre-game small talk and post-game short reactions (“nice shot”, “u carried”, “bruh”).

Timing & typing emulation — add realistic delays and aborted typing: typing start, pause, send. Example timing model:

think_time = normal(mean=1.2s, sd=0.8s) + rand(0–2s)

send partial message 30% of time then full message after 0.5–1.2s

Error injection — occasional typos, autocorrect artifacts, slang, mixed-case. Don't make every message perfectly formatted.

Session & activity variance — players play at different hours. Stagger play windows across time zones, have random idle disconnects, and inconsistent play-session lengths.

Persona depth for a subset — pick 10% of bots and give them 2–3 lines of backstory and specific map/weapons preferences. That subset will anchor believability.

Reduce obvious meta names — rename not_a_bot, NPC_energy, GODCOMPLEX → subtle variants or normal names.

Introduce social behaviors — say “sorry” after teamkill, “gl hf” pre-match sometimes, friendly / trash talk mix.

